Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (Store: Startup, Shutdown, Do; AC5, AC7, AC16, AC22, AC26, supports AC61)
Research: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/research.md Q12 (memory_peak_bytes in the capture stopped line)
Why this approach: a nil-safe captureRun in run.go holds store, sink and budget, so capture off is a nil value and every path (bind failure, serve failed, timed-out and clean shutdown) calls the same stop/close. The store opens between the logger and listen, so a failure is the run's only line and nothing is bound. Recorded in plan.md ("Details fixed in T16").
Alternatives rejected: startGateway putting GATEWAY_CAPTURE_DIR in the env map, as the task line says (every GATEWAY_* var lands in the startup line's env_overrides, which 001's TestRun_StartupLine and TestRun_DefaultsWhenNoConfig assert; the spec keeps 001 assertions unchanged), so the helper sets XDG_DATA_HOME to a temp dir instead and plan.md's Testing strategy says so; logging store.Open's error text (it can carry driver text), so a fixed reason is mapped from the error.
Trade-off / known limit: in-process tests read env from a map, so dropping the helper's line makes run exit 2 on an unresolvable default rather than tripping TestMain; TestMain catches the child binary and any future os-env path. TestCapture_PrincipalLocal checks events too, but the Anthropic adapter has no parser until T20, so today it checks exchange rows only. TestMain points HOME at a temp dir, so binary_test.go gives go build the real HOME to keep its caches. Undrained exchanges don't change the exit code.
Verified by: make verify; go test -race -count=3 on the new tests (TestCapture_DisabledIsPassthrough dir_left_empty / default_dir_not_resolved, TestStore_OpenFailsFast, TestRun_DefaultCaptureDirUnresolvable, TestCapture_PrincipalLocal, TestCapture_ShutdownDrainsQueue queued_stored / stream_ends_during_server_shutdown / undrained_counted, with a capture/store goroutine leak check) and TestBinary_SignalShutdown; tests first failed to build on the missing deps.openStore. Mutations, each reverted: dropping the child's GATEWAY_CAPTURE_DIR made TestMain fail naming <tmp>/llm-gateway; dropping the helper's XDG_DATA_HOME failed 10 001 run tests; stopping capture before srv.Shutdown failed all three ShutdownDrainsQueue subtests. Every 001 cmd/gateway test passes with capture on, assertions unchanged.
